WEBVTT

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:04.250
In this video I want to show how to install CowCatcher.

00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:12.470
There are several ways to get to the website, but the easiest is to type CowCatcher AI.

00:00:13.670 --> 00:00:15.590
Then it shows up on GitHub.

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:24.650
You land on this page, and if you scroll down it says Powered by the AI Detector.

00:00:25.130 --> 00:00:29.090
Below it there is also an explanation of the next steps, but we click here.

00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:34.490
Here under Releases is the latest version.

00:00:35.330 --> 00:00:36.470
So we click that.

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:40.070
Now let's see what we are going to install it on.

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:44.550
I have a Windows computer, so I click this one.

00:00:45.310 --> 00:00:46.790
Then a folder starts downloading.

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:52.710
If you have an Apple computer, such as a Mac mini, you download this version.

00:00:54.940 --> 00:00:58.040
If you have Linux, you install this version.

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:01.540
Otherwise there are no differences in the installation

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:03.100
between Apple and Windows.

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:05.240
Linux works a little differently.

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:08.480
As you can see at the top right, it has been downloaded.

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:11.060
Then we go to Downloads.

00:01:13.370 --> 00:01:14.830
There you can extract it.

00:01:16.410 --> 00:01:17.990
It asks whether you want to extract it.

00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:22.280
Yes, it is doing that now.

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:27.120
Then it opens automatically.

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:33.680
And here we have the program: the AI Detector, the version, Windows.

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:36.060
Then we can click it.

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:38.060
And then it asks:

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:40.340
Hey, this is an unprotected program.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:41.080
Are you sure?

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:44.100
Then you click More info and then Run anyway.

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:50.900
A second way to get around this: right-click the file.

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:52.480
Properties.

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:54.100
And click Unblock.

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:56.220
Then that pop-up does not appear.

00:01:56.900 --> 00:01:58.460
Tick it and then OK.

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:08.020
When you click it, it installs the AI Detector.

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:13.000
So in the background it now starts installing the program.

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:17.600
When the installation is done, you get one more pop-up.

00:02:18.340 --> 00:02:25.980
Here it asks whether the program should start automatically after your computer has been switched off.

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:27.480
This is very handy.

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:32.480
Of course, if your computer goes off, or you switch it off and start it again in the morning,

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:34.420
the program starts again by itself.

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:37.720
If you don't want that, click No.

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:38.660
Do you want it?

00:02:38.660 --> 00:02:40.760
Which is really always the case: click Yes.

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:45.420
And you can always switch it off again by telling the program:

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:48.500
I want to pause detection now.

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:53.420
Finally you get this pop-up asking whether to allow this program.

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:56.820
Then you click Allow.

00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:00.460
In the background you could already see it had started.

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:03.700
This is the AI Detector.

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:08.480
The first time the program starts, it searches for all cameras

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:14.300
connected to your network, so also the cameras you have installed.

00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:16.120
They show up here.

00:03:16.220 --> 00:03:18.220
Well, for me they are all here.

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:20.600
I'm going to add one now.

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:24.480
Then you click Connect cameras.

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:30.700
Then it asks for the password of that camera.

00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:33.760
You can type it in here.

00:03:35.260 --> 00:03:39.600
And if the camera is not in this list, but you have mounted it

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:49.600
and can open it in its app, check in the settings whether the RTSP or ONVIF protocol is switched on.

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:52.780
Here it also says connection failed, because there was no password yet.

00:03:52.780 --> 00:03:57.400
So we try again now.

00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:59.400
It tries to connect to the camera.

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:01.400
It can be opened.

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:03.400
Well, that worked.

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:05.400
We give the camera a name.

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:12.120
In my case this is the back of the barn, looking at the left side.

00:04:12.220 --> 00:04:14.220
Right.

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:16.220
Click Add camera.

00:04:16.220 --> 00:04:18.220
Here we decide: what are we going to do?

00:04:18.220 --> 00:04:20.220
Is it used for calving?

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:22.220
Or for heat?

00:04:22.220 --> 00:04:24.220
So CowCatcher is heat.

00:04:24.220 --> 00:04:26.220
CalvingCatcher is calving.

00:04:26.220 --> 00:04:28.220
And then there is the Tail Up option.

00:04:28.220 --> 00:04:30.220
Which means the tail is raised.

00:04:30.220 --> 00:04:32.220
This is an extension of the calving part.

00:04:32.220 --> 00:04:36.220
Here we really check whether the cow has had her tail up for longer than a set number of minutes.

00:04:36.220 --> 00:04:40.220
Here we really check whether the cow has had her tail up for longer than a set number of minutes.

00:04:40.220 --> 00:04:44.220
Here we really check whether the cow has had her tail up for longer than a set number of minutes.

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:48.220
That is of course a sign that she is about to calve.

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:50.220
And then you get a detection for it.

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:52.220
But here we are going to do heat.

00:04:52.220 --> 00:04:54.220
So we click CowCatcher.

00:04:54.220 --> 00:04:56.220
Here it says update automatically.

00:04:56.220 --> 00:04:58.220
When we have a new model,

00:04:58.220 --> 00:05:00.220
that happens automatically.

00:05:00.220 --> 00:05:02.220
You get it too.

00:05:02.220 --> 00:05:04.220
We call it Heat dairy cows here.

00:05:04.220 --> 00:05:06.220
We call it Heat dairy cows here.

00:05:06.220 --> 00:05:08.220
It applies to the dairy cows.

00:05:08.220 --> 00:05:10.220
It applies to the dairy cows.

00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:12.220
Here we can connect Telegram.

00:05:12.220 --> 00:05:14.220
Here we can connect Telegram.

00:05:14.220 --> 00:05:16.220
It is neatly explained here too.

00:05:16.220 --> 00:05:18.220
For example, if we open BotFather,

00:05:18.220 --> 00:05:20.220
it opens the bot for you right away.

00:05:20.220 --> 00:05:22.220
It opens the bot for you right away.

00:05:22.220 --> 00:05:24.220
Then follow these steps.

00:05:24.220 --> 00:05:26.220
We skip that briefly.

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:28.220
What you get is a very long code.

00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:30.220
An API token.

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:32.220
You fill it in here.

00:05:32.220 --> 00:05:34.220
We send the alert to my phone.

00:05:34.220 --> 00:05:36.220
We send the alert to my phone.

00:05:36.220 --> 00:05:38.220
A group is possible too.

00:05:38.220 --> 00:05:41.530
Then you go to Telegram.

00:05:41.530 --> 00:05:43.530
Connect.

00:05:43.530 --> 00:05:45.530
But it says the bot token is invalid.

00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:47.530
I can't send anything.

00:05:47.530 --> 00:05:49.530
Then you get an alert or an error message.

00:05:49.530 --> 00:05:51.530
We can skip that for now.

00:05:51.530 --> 00:05:53.530
We save the detector.

00:05:53.530 --> 00:05:57.420
We save the detector.

00:05:57.420 --> 00:05:59.420
It works.

00:05:59.420 --> 00:06:05.840
